// The descriptor set of the last occlusion-pyramid pass: the level it reduces and the four levels it writes.

// Builds the last four levels of the camera's occlusion-culling pyramid, from its 32x16 mip four down to the 2x1 top,
// in one 16x8 workgroup: each thread reduces one 2x2 block of mip four to a texel of mip five, kept in workgroup
// memory, and the workgroup reduces those in place through the remaining levels. The levels below hold 16-bit floats
// rounded toward the far plane, and the minimum of such values is one of them, so every level here is exact.
source_level: descriptor<{ type: StorageImage<r16f>, binding: 1033, access: read }>;
level_5: descriptor<{ type: StorageImage<r16f>, binding: 1034, access: write }>;
level_6: descriptor<{ type: StorageImage<r16f>, binding: 1035, access: write }>;
level_7: descriptor<{ type: StorageImage<r16f>, binding: 1036, access: write }>;
level_8: descriptor<{ type: StorageImage<r16f>, binding: 1037, access: write }>;
